    "src/lib/data/codes/flags.test.ts holds the shipped files to this list (a flag cannot be dropped, added or changed without this file changing, and so a reviewer reading it) and holds the TypeScript readers to the answers; tests/python/test_code_flags.py holds gedit_nc.axis_words_of, frame_of and speed_limit_bound_of to the same answers.",
    "axisWords: 'data' = the axis words of the block are values, not positions (coordinate set, shift, centre, tilt angle, dwell time); 'machine' = positions outside the program's frame (machine coordinates, reference points). frame: 'open' / 'close' = the code opens or closes a coordinate frame that is not the program's own; a code whose values decide is 'open'. speedLimitBound: 'upper' is the clamp every speed limit was before M9; 'lower' is a minimum.",
    "droppedByOverride lists the entries a child database replaces with an entry that carries fewer flags than the entry it replaced, each with the reason. An override that drops a flag without a row here fails the test."
